==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Samba Cat''' at Level 10.

Evolves into '''Gato Amigo''' when obtained from [[Boogie Awakens!]] (may drop on the 1st stage but guaranteed on the 2nd) and is at level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Very similar to [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] in terms of usage. Cheap and expendable, Boogie Cat can be summoned en masse to take hits in place of other, more important units. This meatshield role is quite valuable, if not for the wide selection of Cats able to perform this role much better due to faster speed. Boogie Cat, however, can be accessed much earlier than most alternatives and can be used in {{4c}} stages, where there is considerably less competition.

While Boogie Cat's slow movement speed is generally a con, it does have a use in preventing [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] from burrowing or certain slow units from unleashing dangerous attacks, as the likes of [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]] can sometimes slip into the range of an enemy with a powerful [[Omni Strike]] attack, for example, and cause them to attack and ruin everything.

His [[Cat Combo]], [[Feel the Dance (Combo)|Feel the Dance]], can be used in many [[Legend Stages]] stages to great effect, especially later, if the Cats involved are raised to their full potential.

==='''True Form'''===
Gato Amigo's minimal health and range, three knockbacks, Single Target and slowish attack animation often result in his death before he can make any use of his Knockback ability. The only notable enemies for which it might be useful are [[One Horn]], [[Cyberhorn]], [[Oldhorn]], [[Kid Tappa]], [[Li'l Zyclone]], [[Miss Haka]] and [[Big Sal]], due to their low range. Even then, it's still only a 5% chance, meaning Amigo may not even knockback no matter what setup you use. The knockback itself can be quite deadly on stages like [[Mineral Treatment]], where it can interrupt your stalling efforts.

For early [[Uncanny Legends]], Gato Amigo does work as a short-term counter to Oldhorn. In stages such as [[Annin Pass]], [[Utsubobo Seamount]] and [[Seahorse Siren]], there is not a large amount of them to counter, making his Single Target attack less of a problem.

==='''Talents'''===
With Talents, Gato Amigo can become one of the only [[Surge Immunity|Surge-Immune]] meatshields in the game. Due to his slowness, he can't completely prevent most [[:Category:Surge Attack Enemies|Surge Attackers]] from advancing, but his spammability can greatly reduce the amount of ground lost when a Surge hits your frontlines. This is especially useful against [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku Enemies]], many of which can produce Surges deep in your lines when slain. Use him with Talented [[Actress Cat (Special Cat)|Beefcake Cat]] or Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)| Li'l King Dragon]] for an excellent anti-Surge combo. He combos excellently with [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] to create an impenetrable wall of surge immune meatshields.

Knockback Up by itself isn't really useful and could actually be detrimental depending on the stages where you're bringing Gato Amigo in. If you happen to own a Death Mini-Surge Ability Orb, this talent can be upgraded to serve as a backup tool in case enemies start pushing too hard, where a lucky Mini-Surge could instantly regain whatever ground you lost. Even with how unreliable the Mini-Surge itself is due to spawning right where your cats would be as well as the 15% chance for the Knockback succeeding in the first place, this gives Gato Amigo a lot more use to ease the pressure in a lot of stages.

Resist Slow and Resist Freeze, as with almost all Resist talents, are utterly worthless and should not even be considered for investment, while HP Buff is sadly not that great, despite the 80% buff, due to Gato Amigo's inherently awful stats.

==='''Orb'''===
Cannon Recharge Ability Orb is a best option for such a cheap and low-cooldown meatshield. Dodge Attack could potentially be good for general stalling. Lastly Death Mini-Surge, if you upgraded Knockback Up talent, but it still usually procs only once every 10 Boogies, and can potentially miss.

