==Trivia==
*If you look closely, Boogie Cat's afro will come off when knocked back, meaning that his hair is a wig and he is bald.
**This is still present in the Nintendo 3DS version.
*Gato Amigo means "Cat Friend" in Spanish.
*Even though his name is already Spanish, Gato Amigo is renamed to Gato Mariachi in the Spanish translation of [[The Battle Cats]].
*In The Battle Cats Unite!, since its True Form is currently unused, if one were to edit their save file to add it in, they can see that Gato Amigo does not have Zombie targeting, making it and [[Driller Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Driller Cat]] the only two units in the game that share this phenomenon.
*Prior to [[Version 15.6 Update|Version 15.6]], Boogie Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Boogie Cat
No one can stop the beats!
Cheap to produce. Comes with bonus groove.
It's boogie time! Go! Go! Cat!</pre>
<pre>Samba Cat
Beats have brought this one to eleven!
Cheap and fast to produce. Everybody dance!
Dance til you drop! Sammmbaaaaa!!111one</pre>
<pre>Gato Amigo
Out to bring joy to the senoritas of the world.
He's never been to Mexico, he's just a Mariachi
nerd. Can send enemies flying!</pre>
*The "Sammmbaaaaa!!111one" in Samba Cat's description was a reference to [https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/the-1-phenomenon The "!1" Phenomenon], which occurs when typing a string of exclamation points and letting go of the shift key too early.

